The key distinction
Term	Question it answers
Test object	What exactly am I testing?
Test basis	What information tells me what it should do?
Test condition	Which aspect of it am I checking?
Test scenario	Which situation/flow am I testing?
Test case	How exactly will I test it?
Expected result	What should happen?
Actual result	What actually happened?
Test oracle	How do I know what is correct?
Defect	What is wrong?
Risk	What could go wrong and how serious is it?
Test level	At which level am I testing?
Test type	Which characteristic am I evaluating?

For your QA learning, Test object → Test basis → Test condition → Test scenario → Test case is an especially useful sequence to understand. It prevents the common beginner mistake of jumping straight from a user story to writing test cases without first understanding what the actual testing target and risks are.

